; Find a named object out of reach and say where it is
;
; Try a rejected noun phrase as a place or as any object.
; .
; The words fitted no object of the kind the command takes. A noun phrase can
; still be a place of the exits of the actor's location ("take lonelands") or
; an object of another kind, such as a person for a verb that wants a thing
; ("eat Gandalf"). The routine looks for the words first among the exits, then
; among all the objects (AllMode ANY, within reach unless AllActive is set). If one is found it becomes
; the noun and the command is refused with "You cannot {verb} {noun}." (#R$711A
; with ActionAllowed 0, so the sentence #R$712B goes to the input window). If
; none is found the message "I do not see {THING} here" is printed, the
; address of the typed words being the {THING}.
; .
; Entered from #R$7D98 as well.
; .
; HL The typed noun phrase (RecBuf1 or RecBuf2)
; DE Variable to receive the found noun (FirstObject or SecondObject)
; BC Variable of the noun's kind (Noun1Kind or Noun2Kind), set here
; O:A 0
; O:F Z
@label=FindNounElsewhere
c$7DFE PUSH HL       ;
 $7DFF CALL $9E95    ; SeekActorExits
@isub=LD A,NOUN_PLACE
 $7E02 LD A,$01      ;
 $7E04 LD (BC),A     ; the noun is a place
 $7E05 CALL $9EA0    ; FindExitByName
@isub=CP END_MARK
 $7E08 CP $FF        ;
 $7E0A JR NZ,$7E20   ; found
 $7E0C POP HL        ;
@isub=LD A,ALL_MODE_ANY
 $7E0D LD A,$02      ;
 $7E0F LD ($B710),A  ; AllMode: any kind of object
@isub=LD IX,ObjectTable-3
 $7E12 LD IX,$C060   ;
 $7E16 XOR A         ;
 $7E17 LD (BC),A     ; the noun is an object
 $7E18 PUSH HL       ; kept for the message
 $7E19 CALL $9DD9    ; FindNextNamedObject
@isub=CP END_MARK
 $7E1C CP $FF        ;
 $7E1E JR Z,$7E25    ; nothing of that name
*$7E20 POP HL        ;
 $7E21 LD (DE),A     ; the noun
 $7E22 JP $711A      ; StartPerform: "You cannot ..."
*$7E25 CALL $7D6B    ; SetPerformMode
 $7E28 LD HL,$ADD3   ; "I do not see {THING} here"
 $7E2B CALL $72D3    ;
 $7E2E XOR A         ;
 $7E2F RET           ;
